<p>You're right, I'm sorry. I'll provide actual commentary here.</p>
<p>My first question going into an article is &quot;Is the anomaly interesting?&quot; In this case, the answer is a solid no. I've been trying not to be reactionarily negative to GAW articles &#8212; it's here to stay, whether or not I like it &#8212; but I still don't like their version of the Misters, just as I don't like the fact that Wondertainment's were all given articles as well. And this is a guy with no personality &#8212; quite a few GAW Misters have gotten an upvote from me because of their personalities! &#8212; who sucks people into his ass; it's stupid.</p>
<p>Barring that, the next question is, &quot;Is the story being told worth reading?&quot; I mean, addenda and documentation can really make up for a lackluster item or description. But once I saw it was just more babbling by the GAW characters, who I can't keep straight and who I don't particularly care about, not to mention there's just <em>so much here</em>, I had no interest in reading further to find out if it was worth my time.</p>
<p>So this is a swing and a miss, as far as I'm concerned.</p>

