			<div class="content" id="post-content-2818066">
									

<p>I think the worst part about it isn't that it's about memes, but it's about something even less interesting to you than memes.</p>
<p>You have a point there, with the story, even if it does jab at pathos for people like me who are already invested. It doesn't really make <strong>sense</strong> for the SCP document to contain these anecdotes because they have nothing to do with the anomaly itself. It has brainstorming about what the SCP should be, but not how it was made.</p>
<p>I think it'd be pretty funny if the SCP wasn't the asshole portal mannequin and was instead the place it lead to. &quot;Currently, only AO-███, AO-███, and SCP-████ are contained there due to their anomalous properties.&quot; So what is the anomalous property of this safehouse? Could this be elaborated on? Is there anything weird about this safehouse besides &quot;This anartist wants the SCP foundation to pay attention to him.&quot; I understand the mister was lazily put together, and making the soulless sexy old man any more interesting would clash with the disillusionment of the anartist but there needs to be <strong>something</strong> interesting about it. Or maybe it could be JJ himself that's the SCP. I don't know. My mind is easily swayed.</p>
<p>Since SCP-3012 was posted so recently, I'm sort of wondering if there's some sort of theme I should be concerned about.</p>

